Build the nixfmt executable on Windows.

Upstream: NixOS/nixfmt v1.2.0 (https://github.com/NixOS/nixfmt/tree/v1.2.0).
Not yet submitted upstream; written to be (see packages/source/nixfmt/repro.nim
in reprobuild-packages for the assessment). Every change is either guarded by
`mingw32_HOST_OS` / `os(windows)` or is a no-op on POSIX.

* nixfmt.cabal: depend on `unix` only off Windows (`unix` declares itself
  unbuildable there), and list the new System.Interrupt module. Relax
  `filepath < 1.5` to `< 1.6` -- upstream dropped the bound in 1.3.0 -- so
  GHC 9.12's own filepath satisfies it rather than cabal rebuilding filepath
  and every boot package above it.
* main/System/Interrupt.hs (new): the SIGINT handler Main installed
  (System.Posix.Signals / exitImmediately), off Windows only; on Windows GHC's
  runtime turns Ctrl-C into an exception, which System.IO.Atomic's rollback
  already handles. A module of its own so that only it needs CPP: CPP in
  Main.hs would break the string gaps in its help texts.
* main/System/IO/Atomic.hs: on Windows, carry the original file's
  permissions over with System.Directory instead of POSIX mode and owner.
* main/System/IO/Utf8.hs, main/Main.hs: open files and standard handles with
  `noNewlineTranslation`, so Windows writes LF exactly as POSIX does instead of
  turning every LF into CRLF. A no-op on POSIX, where it is already the mode.

